Both branches (Operand 2 and Operand 3) must be compatible with the target assignment type. If the two operands have different numeric types, the Java compiler applies binary numeric promotion to harmonize them to a common super-type:

```java
boolean condition = true;
Number num = condition ? Integer.valueOf(1) : Double.valueOf(2.5); // Unified type

// SUBTLE TRAP: Numeric promotion to double
Object obj = true ? 1 : 2.0; 
System.out.println(obj); // Prints 1.0 (promoted to Double, not Integer 1!)
```

