sections.content:
Instead of wrapping large loop bodies in deep `if` statements, use `continue` at the top of the loop as a guard clause to filter out unwanted items early:

```java
// Deep nesting anti-pattern
for (User user : users) {
    if (user != null) {
        if (user.isActive()) {
            if (user.hasValidEmail()) {
                // 4 levels indented!
            }
        }
    }
}

// Clean Guard Clause Pattern using continue
for (User user : users) {
    if (user == null || !user.isActive() || !user.hasValidEmail()) continue;

    // Main processing stays flat at indent level 1!
    sendNotification(user);
}
```

