Any `for` loop can be mechanically transformed into an equivalent `while` loop:

```java
// for loop
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) { System.out.println(i); }

// Equivalent while loop
int i = 0;              // 1. Initialization
while (i < 5) {         // 2. Condition
    System.out.println(i);
    i++;                // 3. Update
}
```

Rule of Thumb: Use `for` when iterating over fixed ranges/indices; use `while` when looping depends on dynamic state, user input, or mathematical convergence.

