Swapping elements at index `i` and `j` is a cornerstone of sorting and array reversal algorithms:

```java
// Step 1: Stash value of arr[i] in temp
int temp = arr[i];
// Step 2: Overwrite arr[i] with arr[j]
arr[i] = arr[j];
// Step 3: Write stashed temp value into arr[j]
arr[j] = temp;
```

