sections.content:
Under the hood in modern Java (Java 9+), a String is backed by a compact byte array:

```java
public final class String {
    private final byte[] value; // Raw byte storage
    private final byte coder;   // LATIN1 (1 byte/char) or UTF16 (2 bytes/char)
    private int hash;           // Cached hash code (defaults to 0)
}
```
If a String contains only ASCII/Latin-1 characters, Java stores each character using just 1 byte instead of 2 bytes, cutting heap memory consumption by up to 50%!

