GROUP BY collapses rows: one output row per group. A window function computes over a set of related rows (the window) but keeps every row. The OVER(...) clause defines the window:
PARTITION BY splits it into groups (like GROUP BY, but nothing is collapsed);
ORDER BY orders rows inside each partition.

