In a 2D grid, each cell is a vertex and edges connect it to its up, down, left and right neighbours. You rarely build an adjacency list; just loop over the directions:
int[][] dirs = {{1,0},{-1,0},{0,1},{0,-1}};
Islands, mazes, flood fill and the shortest path in a matrix are all graph problems.

